WEBVTT
Language: en

1
00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:15.933
Each letter is a vector path from a font bundled with Lantern; no installed font is asked for. Write traces every contour. The close-up shows one glyph’s points and handles.

2
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:35.167
The shaper gives every glyph an exact advance; the ticks mark each pen position and the brace spans the measured width. The boxed letters are Inter’s widest and narrowest; in JetBrains Mono every glyph has the same advance.

3
00:00:40.433 --> 00:00:57.700
TransformMatchingShapes pairs glyphs whose outlines are the same path once each is centred and scaled to one size, so position and size do not count. Every glyph pairs with its own copy at 60% size; across the two fonts nothing pairs, not even the same letter.

4
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:18.600
The font stores quadratic curves and lines, as the note beside it counts. Lantern raises every segment to a cubic, so one kind of path feeds both the SVG player and offline video frames.

5
00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:38.367
TransformMatchingText pairs glyphs of the same letter, longest runs first. The glyphs of cache and the i travel down into the new word, the crossed m and both s glyphs shrink away, and the underlined h and t grow in.

6
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:57.700
The pen-and-ink style asks for EB Garamond, but Lantern draws labels in embedded Inter, stretched to the width agentic-mermaid wrote into each label’s textLength. Box shapes and strokes come from the style; only the letterforms differ.
